  "data": {
    "body": "When a falling object reaches terminal speed, its kinetic energy reaches a constant value. However, the gravitational potential energy of the system consisting of the object, Earth and atmosphere continues to decrease. Which of the following best describes why this is not a violation of the conservation of energy for the system consisting of the object plus the Earth?",
